## Context (original request — preserved)

CC completed the P1 implementation as inspect-and-propose (W1–W8, two ADRs, MemoryId map, 10-case test
plan) and **did not commit** (boundary held). The pass surfaced a **build-stopping blocker** that
supersedes packet entry-condition **E1** and reopens the engine. The code was statically reasoned; the
build aborts at dependency resolution. Three decisions were needed before P1 could build, test, and move
to CD/Claude diff review + human commit.

**Compile blocker vs. acceptance gates.** Decision 1 is the compile blocker — it blocks dependency
resolution (and therefore all build/test) and invalidates v0.4.0 as the P1 entry pin. Decisions 2–3 are
P1-acceptance gates (evidence-scope / wording); they must be settled before P1 is accepted, but do not
have to delay the engine re-pin starting.

### Decision 1 — v0.4.1 engine re-pin (the blocker, Divergence #1)

**Problem.** `mktd02-v0.4.0` pins ic-cdk 0.17 / is 0.6; the `open-chatZD` workspace is on ic-cdk 0.18 /
is 0.7. Two failures: (a) **resolution-fatal** — ic-cdk 0.17 and 0.18 both pull `ic-cdk-executor`
declaring the same `links` value, which Cargo forbids in one graph; (b) **type-level** —
`MemoryManager<DefaultMemoryImpl>` from is-0.6 ≠ is-0.7, crossing the `mktd02::init` shared-manager
boundary (W6).

**Proposed fix.** Re-pin the engine to ic-cdk 0.18 + is 0.7, re-release as `mktd02-v0.4.1`; P1 re-points
its pin to v0.4.1.

**Scope / risk weighed:** breaking dep releases (real engine work — own build + lib 9/9 + PocketIC 3/3 +
release gate); DaffyDefs blast radius (single line vs frozen); E4 re-confirmation under is-0.7;
tag-classification test (patch only if protocol / receipt schema / hash formulas / 8-slot 100–107 layout
unchanged).

### Decision 2 — Q1: message-body certification scope (high-assurance / evidence)

`get_state_bytes()` builds its preimage from a bounded heap projection + a direct-chat counterparts
summary + a tombstone sentinel — message **bodies are not in the certified preimage**. Physical body
purge is deferred GC (reusing `delete_direct_chat`). Synchrony is met because the sentinel / heap
projection flip within the same update call. Certifies the state transition, **not** physical body
absence (final erasure is the P3 uninstall, after receipt export). Requires the P4/RTS copy to say so.

### Decision 3 — W1A: V3 module-hash interim

`mktd02::init` / `on_post_upgrade` wired with an additive `mktd_module_hash: Option<[u8;32]>`.
`None → [0u8;32]` does not satisfy V3. Full V3 needs the installer (`local_user_index`) to supply the
real module hash — out of P1 scope. Interim: two-pass attestation; receipts disclosed as V1–V2 (V3
pending) until the installer wiring lands.

